WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:01.067 line:92%
-We're back with Tina Fey.

00:00:01.067 --> 00:00:03.770
Congratulations on the "Kimm
Schmidt" interactive special

00:00:03.770 --> 00:00:06.806 align:start size:94% position:6%
What gave you
the idea or the impetus

00:00:06.806 --> 00:00:09.676 align:start size:94% position:6%
to do a choose-your-own
adventure "Kimmy Schmidt"?

00:00:09.676 --> 00:00:11.244
-Yes, well, first of all,
legally I think we're not

00:00:11.244 --> 00:00:13.113 align:start size:94% position:6%
allowed to refer to it as
"choose your own adventure."

00:00:13.113 --> 00:00:16.716
-Gotcha. Well, I think legally
I can call it whatever I want.

00:00:16.716 --> 00:00:19.386 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You can -- You can go nuts.
[ Laughs ]

00:00:19.386 --> 00:00:25.091
But what happened was, we were
finishing shooting the series,

00:00:25.091 --> 00:00:26.559 size:84% position:42% line:92%
the body of the series,

00:00:26.559 --> 00:00:28.228 align:start size:94% position:6%
and right as we were
finishing up

00:00:28.228 --> 00:00:29.629 align:start size:94% position:6%
that last part
of that last season,

00:00:29.629 --> 00:00:33.666
Netflix came to us and said,
"We have this technology that --

00:00:33.666 --> 00:00:35.301 line:92%
We're about to do this sho

00:00:35.301 --> 00:00:37.337 align:start size:94% position:6%
called 'Bandersnatch'
on 'Black Mirror,'" which --

00:00:37.337 --> 00:00:39.072 align:start size:94% position:6%
I don't know if
you saw "Bandersnatch."

00:00:39.072 --> 00:00:40.740 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I did.
-It was a really cool

00:00:40.740 --> 00:00:43.810 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Black Mirror" special
that was a very dark, moody,

00:00:43.810 --> 00:00:46.312 align:start size:94% position:6%
super-cool version
of this technology

00:00:46.312 --> 00:00:48.782
where you're watching it
and then you, the viewer,

00:00:48.782 --> 00:00:51.985 align:start size:94% position:6%
with your remote, make choices
of what the character does

00:00:51.985 --> 00:00:53.953 align:start size:94% position:6%
And they said --
They showed it to us early

00:00:53.953 --> 00:00:57.424 align:start size:94% position:6%
which was really cool,
and then they said,

00:00:57.424 --> 00:01:00.360 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Do you think you could do thi
with 'Kimmy Schmidt'?"

00:01:00.360 --> 00:01:02.962 line:92%
And we were like, "120 percent,"

00:01:02.962 --> 00:01:06.833 align:start size:94% position:6%
because, one, it just
was such exciting technology

00:01:06.833 --> 00:01:10.403 align:start size:94% position:6%
and, two, our show
is kind of known for

00:01:10.403 --> 00:01:12.405 line:92%
kind of having too many jokes...

00:01:12.405 --> 00:01:13.840 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes.
-...going on.

00:01:13.840 --> 00:01:19.012 align:start size:94% position:6%
And so it was a way to write
as many jokes as you want

00:01:19.012 --> 00:01:22.348 align:start size:94% position:6%
but not choke people with them
all at once.

00:01:22.348 --> 00:01:26.152 align:start size:94% position:6%
So if you --
This is an interactive special

00:01:26.152 --> 00:01:28.188 align:start size:94% position:6%
We've called it a movie a lot.
I don't know.

00:01:28.188 --> 00:01:29.589 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's called
an interactive special.

00:01:29.589 --> 00:01:34.527 align:start size:94% position:6%
And basically Kimmy is about t
get married to a royal --

00:01:34.527 --> 00:01:37.230 align:start size:94% position:6%
a British royal, distant
British royal named Frederick.

00:01:37.230 --> 00:01:39.999 align:start size:94% position:6%
Prince Frederick, who is playe
by Daniel Radcliffe,

00:01:39.999 --> 00:01:41.101 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
who's awesome.

00:01:41.101 --> 00:01:44.671 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then in time she finds out
that the reverend --

00:01:44.671 --> 00:01:47.407 align:start size:94% position:6%
She makes a discovery
that makes her concerned

00:01:47.407 --> 00:01:49.175 align:start size:94% position:6%
that there's another bunke
somewhere

00:01:49.175 --> 00:01:51.311
that hasn't been discovered,
so she has to make some choice

00:01:51.311 --> 00:01:55.115 align:start size:94% position:6%
as to how far she'll go to try
to find this other bunker,

00:01:55.115 --> 00:01:58.718 align:start size:94% position:6%
and you get to make
these choices with her.

00:01:58.718 --> 00:02:00.420 align:start size:94% position:6%
Now, you also
get to make choices --

00:02:00.420 --> 00:02:01.721 align:start size:94% position:6%
You'll appreciate this
as a writer,

00:02:01.721 --> 00:02:04.190 align:start size:94% position:6%
'cause Netflix was like,
"You know, so, 'Bandersnatch

00:02:04.190 --> 00:02:06.693 align:start size:94% position:6%
was one story,
so you'll probably want

00:02:06.693 --> 00:02:07.527 size:88% position:44% line:92%
to keep it to one story,

00:02:07.527 --> 00:02:09.395 align:start size:94% position:6%
because it's
pretty impossible to track."

00:02:09.395 --> 00:02:13.533
We were like, "Cool, cool, cool.
So three stories."

00:02:13.533 --> 00:02:15.201 align:start size:94% position:6%
-[ Laughs ]
-We were just so used to

00:02:15.201 --> 00:02:18.171 size:81% position:41%
Being able to cut away
to the other story...

00:02:18.171 --> 00:02:19.739 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Sure.
-...like, momentum-wise.

00:02:19.739 --> 00:02:22.041 align:start size:94% position:6%
Please hold. There's
a colonial lady coming in.

00:02:22.041 --> 00:02:23.576 size:75% position:38% line:92%
Yes. Can I help you?

00:02:23.576 --> 00:02:24.978 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-[ Laughs ]

00:02:24.978 --> 00:02:27.881 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm sorry.
You're not making sound. What?

00:02:27.881 --> 00:02:31.017 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm -- Yes. Hello.
-Hello.

00:02:31.017 --> 00:02:33.253 align:start size:94% position:6%
-We're taping
a television program.

00:02:33.253 --> 00:02:35.088 size:81% position:41% line:92%
Do you need something?

00:02:35.088 --> 00:02:40.793
-I did the interactive --
I clicked for her entry.

00:02:40.793 --> 00:02:42.529 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-[ Giggling ]

00:02:42.529 --> 00:02:45.064 align:start size:94% position:6%
-The colonial lady
just called us losers!

00:02:45.064 --> 00:02:47.834 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Wait a second!
We're not losers!

00:02:47.834 --> 00:02:50.703 align:start size:94% position:6%
-This means "loyalists"
in colonial times,

00:02:50.703 --> 00:02:52.572 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
so that's on you!

00:02:52.572 --> 00:02:56.543 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Hold on. Um...

00:02:56.543 --> 00:02:58.945 align:start size:94% position:6%
So -- Oh, wait.
So did you say you played it

00:02:58.945 --> 00:03:02.182 align:start size:94% position:6%
-There's a joke --
This really speaks back

00:03:02.182 --> 00:03:05.185 align:start size:94% position:6%
to how you layer jokes
on jokes on jokes.

00:03:05.185 --> 00:03:09.355 align:start size:94% position:6%
Even the theme song
has a joke in it.

00:03:09.355 --> 00:03:11.658 size:84% position:42% line:92%
-Yes. Should we -- Hmm.

00:03:11.658 --> 00:03:13.726 align:start size:94% position:6%
I don't know
if we should give it away.

00:03:13.726 --> 00:03:15.962
-You don't have to give it away,
but I guess the --

00:03:15.962 --> 00:03:18.431
-But I will say, though, there's
the thing with the theme song,

00:03:18.431 --> 00:03:23.069 align:start size:94% position:6%
that if you -- like any
Netflix show, when it starts

00:03:23.069 --> 00:03:25.471 align:start size:94% position:6%
you have the option
to skip intro.

00:03:25.471 --> 00:03:27.807 align:start size:94% position:6%
And, you know,
my husband, Jeff Richmond,

00:03:27.807 --> 00:03:32.612
one of our EPs on the show
also wrote that theme song

00:03:32.612 --> 00:03:33.513 size:84% position:42% line:92%
which I think is one of

00:03:33.513 --> 00:03:35.148 align:start size:94% position:6%
the greatest TV theme song
of all time.

00:03:35.148 --> 00:03:37.383
-It is one of the greatest
TV theme songs of all time

00:03:37.383 --> 00:03:38.885 align:start size:94% position:6%
I completely echo
that sentiment.

00:03:38.885 --> 00:03:42.956 align:start size:94% position:6%
And yet, I imagine that if you
watch a bunch in a row...

00:03:42.956 --> 00:03:45.491 align:start size:94% position:6%
like, you might at some poin
maybe go like,

00:03:45.491 --> 00:03:46.459 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Oh, I'll skip the song."
-Right.

00:03:46.459 --> 00:03:49.362
Or if you're my older daughter
and your dad wrote that song

00:03:49.362 --> 00:03:51.931
and you've heard it a lot of
times just being re-recorded

00:03:51.931 --> 00:03:53.066 line:92%
around the house, you might --

00:03:53.066 --> 00:03:55.902
Because I was showing it
to my older daughter early

00:03:55.902 --> 00:03:57.971 align:start size:94% position:6%
an early copy,
and the theme song came up

00:03:57.971 --> 00:03:59.973
and "skip intro" came up,
and she literally, like,

00:03:59.973 --> 00:04:04.744
looked around to make sure
that her dad was not aroun

00:04:04.744 --> 00:04:05.945 line:92%
and then hit "skip intro,"

00:04:05.945 --> 00:04:08.314
and I knew that there was,
like, a surprise coming.

00:04:08.314 --> 00:04:10.984 align:start size:94% position:6%
There's -- Something
slightly punitive happens

00:04:10.984 --> 00:04:12.919 line:92%
when you hit "skip intro."

00:04:12.919 --> 00:04:14.921 size:84% position:42% line:92%
So...watch that unfold.

00:04:14.921 --> 00:04:20.526
-You are actually going to
head over to 30 Rock today

00:04:20.526 --> 00:04:24.464 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes, I think by the time
me and you are talking on TV

00:04:24.464 --> 00:04:26.065 line:92%
I will have already been there

00:04:26.065 --> 00:04:28.334 align:start size:94% position:6%
We're doing a --
I guess it's a telethon.

00:04:28.334 --> 00:04:30.303 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-It's the "Rise Up New York!

00:04:30.303 --> 00:04:32.672 line:92%
telethon tonight at 7:00 p.m

00:04:32.672 --> 00:04:33.806 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
And I am going down

00:04:33.806 --> 00:04:37.377
to kind of host the live portion
of it from NBC.

00:04:37.377 --> 00:04:40.179 align:start size:94% position:6%
I feel really excited
and privileged

00:04:40.179 --> 00:04:44.150 align:start size:94% position:6%
to get -- to go into NBC.
You know, I think --

00:04:44.150 --> 00:04:48.187 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm sure you feel the same way
that we just long to be --

00:04:48.187 --> 00:04:51.491 align:start size:94% position:6%
The only way
we remotely know how to help

00:04:51.491 --> 00:04:55.762 line:92%
is to go on TV and try to talk

00:04:55.762 --> 00:04:58.197 align:start size:94% position:6%
So I'm going to go down ther
today and hopefully read

00:04:58.197 --> 00:05:00.500 align:start size:94% position:6%
some impressive
fundraising totals.

00:05:00.500 --> 00:05:03.436 size:88% position:44%
-That's great. Thank you
so much for doing that.

00:05:03.436 --> 00:05:06.139 align:start size:94% position:6%
And we will put up
the information,

00:05:06.139 --> 00:05:08.074 align:start size:94% position:6%
because that will have happene
before our show,

00:05:08.074 --> 00:05:11.477 align:start size:94% position:6%
but we'll put it up now if
people want to donate to that.

00:05:11.477 --> 00:05:14.180 align:start size:94% position:6%
And it is always such a deligh
to talk to you, Tina.

00:05:14.180 --> 00:05:15.581 align:start size:94% position:6%
Thank you so much
for being here.

00:05:15.581 --> 00:05:18.818 align:start size:94% position:6%
Do not miss
"Kimmy Schmidt Interactive."

00:05:18.818 --> 00:05:20.253 line:92%
It's fantastic. It's on Netflix.

00:05:20.253 --> 00:05:23.690 align:start size:94% position:6%
We'll be right back
with more "Late Night."

